[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186166847 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e" :question/id #uuid "9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-147885" :question/problem "The disjoint union ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔{A}_{3}⊔{A}_{4}$ of events ${A}_{1},{A}_{2},{A}_{3},{A}_{4}$ covers the entire sample space. Compute $P({A}_{2}|B)$ given the following probabilities:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P(B|{A}_{1})=0.25, & P({A}_{1})=0.28 \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{2})=0.3, &  \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{3})=0.28, & P({A}_{3})=0.18 \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{4})=0.1, & P({A}_{4})=0.22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If the disjoint union ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔…⊔{A}_{n}$ covers the entire sample space, Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability gives us the following:\n\n$$\nP({A}_{k}|B)=\\frac{P(B|{A}_{k})P({A}_{k})}{P(B)}=\\frac{P(B|{A}_{k})P({A}_{k})}{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}P(B|{A}_{i})P({A}_{i})}\n$$\n\nwhere $k=1,2,…,n.$\n\nIn our case, $n=4,$ and ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔{A}_{3}⊔{A}_{4}$ covers the entire sample space. Consequently, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}_{1})+P({A}_{2})+P({A}_{3})+P({A}_{4})=1.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}_{2}) & =1-(P({A}_{1})+P({A}_{3})+P({A}_{4})) \\\\  & =1-(0.28+0.18+0.22) \\\\  & =0.32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}_{2}|B) & =\\frac{P(B|{A}_{2})P({A}_{2})}{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}P(B|{A}_{i})P({A}_{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(B|{A}_{2})P({A}_{2})}{P(B|{A}_{1})P({A}_{1})+P(B|{A}_{2})P({A}_{2})+P(B|{A}_{3})P({A}_{3})+P(B|{A}_{4})P({A}_{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.3)(0.32)}{(0.25)(0.28)+(0.3)(0.32)+(0.28)(0.18)+(0.1)(0.22)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.096}{0.2384} \\\\  & ≈0.403.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3abf36e3-3cf2-5339-8e78-9d57d7acb48a" "answer-408cef73-e79b-5f84-909b-bb78b0af2709" "answer-161fb25c-96cf-5b02-8d7d-25af5ca8f28a" "answer-cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d" "answer-c7987182-3703-5340-83e1-52554f33e28f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3abf36e3-3cf2-5339-8e78-9d57d7acb48a" :answer/id #uuid "3abf36e3-3cf2-5339-8e78-9d57d7acb48a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.286" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-408cef73-e79b-5f84-909b-bb78b0af2709" :answer/id #uuid "408cef73-e79b-5f84-909b-bb78b0af2709" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.322" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-161fb25c-96cf-5b02-8d7d-25af5ca8f28a" :answer/id #uuid "161fb25c-96cf-5b02-8d7d-25af5ca8f28a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.365" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d" :answer/id #uuid "cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.403" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7987182-3703-5340-83e1-52554f33e28f" :answer/id #uuid "c7987182-3703-5340-83e1-52554f33e28f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.444" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166877 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc" :question/id #uuid "095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc" :question/math-academy-id "q-148082" :question/problem "A medical center is investigating the correlation between scoliosis and sports practice in a sample of children.\n\n- $25%$ of children in the sample don't practice sports, and $3%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\n- $30%$ of children in the sample practice one sport, and $2.5%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\n- $45%$ of children in the sample practice two sports, and $3.3%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\nIf $52%$ of children in the entire sample are female, and $2%$ of female children have scoliosis, what is the probability that a randomly chosen child with scoliosis is female? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $F$ be the event that a child is female, $C$ be the event that a child has scoliosis, and ${S}_{0},{S}_{1},{S}_{2}$ be the event that a child practice $0,$ $1,$ or $2$ sports, respectively.\n\nLet's break down the information given in the problem statement:\n\n- From the bullet points, we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P({S}_{0})=0.25 &  & P(C|{S}_{0})=0.03 \\\\  & P({S}_{1})=0.30 &  & P(C|{S}_{1})=0.025 \\\\  & P({S}_{2})=0.45 &  & P(C|{S}_{2})=0.033\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe disjoint union ${S}_{0}⊔{S}_{1}⊔{S}_{2}$ covers the entire sample space, and we have\n\n$$\nP({S}_{0})+P({S}_{1})+P({S}_{2})=0.25+0.30+0.45=1.\n$$\n\n- Since $52%$ of children in the entire sample are female, we have\n\n$$\nP(F)=0.52.\n$$\n\n- Since $2%$ of females have scoliosis, we have\n\n$$\nP(C|F)=0.02.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that a randomly chosen child with scoliosis is female, which is represented as $P(F|C).$ \n\nUsing Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F|C) & =\\frac{P(C|F)P(F)}{P(C)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(C|F)P(F)}{P(C|{S}_{0})P({S}_{0})+P(C|{S}_{1})P({S}_{1})+P(C|{S}_{2})P({S}_{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.02)(0.52)}{(0.03)(0.25)+(0.025)(0.3)+(0.033)(0.45)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.0104}{0.0299} \\\\  & ≈0.348,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/id #uuid "af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460" :answer-field/choices ["answer-144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460" "answer-39018054-1073-5cec-87c0-3be506864193" "answer-7aae2ee8-a81d-50e2-98ea-e2df978f83a9" "answer-85700ac7-cad1-590c-a143-b418ccc70b5b" "answer-7dd4d43d-b30b-5f97-8032-3941bf17d1fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460" :answer/id #uuid "144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.348" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39018054-1073-5cec-87c0-3be506864193" :answer/id #uuid "39018054-1073-5cec-87c0-3be506864193" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.415" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7aae2ee8-a81d-50e2-98ea-e2df978f83a9" :answer/id #uuid "7aae2ee8-a81d-50e2-98ea-e2df978f83a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85700ac7-cad1-590c-a143-b418ccc70b5b" :answer/id #uuid "85700ac7-cad1-590c-a143-b418ccc70b5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dd4d43d-b30b-5f97-8032-3941bf17d1fb" :answer/id #uuid "7dd4d43d-b30b-5f97-8032-3941bf17d1fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.552" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166848 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe" :question/id #uuid "1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-148271" :question/problem "A medical center is investigating the correlation between scoliosis and sports practice in a sample of children.\n\n- $25%$ of children in the sample don't practice sports, and $2.5%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\n- $30%$ of children in the sample practice one sport.\n\n- $45%$ of children in the sample practice two sports, and $2.8%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\nIf $48%$ of children in the entire sample are female, $2.6%$ of female children have scoliosis, and $46%$ of children with scoliosis are female, what is the probability that a randomly chosen child who practices one sport has scoliosis? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $F$ be the event that a child is female, $C$ be the event that a child has scoliosis, and ${S}_{0},{S}_{1},{S}_{2}$ be the event that a child practices $0,$ $1,$ or $2$ sports, respectively.\n\nLet's break down the information given in the problem statement:\n\n- From the bullet points, we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P({S}_{0})=0.25 &  & P(C∣{S}_{0})=0.025 \\\\  & P({S}_{1})=0.30 \\\\  & P({S}_{2})=0.45 &  & P(C∣{S}_{2})=0.028\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe disjoint union ${S}_{0}⊔{S}_{1}⊔{S}_{2}$ covers the entire sample space, and we have\n\n$$\nP({S}_{0})+P({S}_{1})+P({S}_{2})=0.25+0.30+0.45=1.\n$$\n\n- Since $48%$ of students in the entire sample are female, we have\n\n$$\nP(F)=0.48.\n$$\n\n- Since $2.6%$ of females have scoliosis, we have\n\n$$\nP(C∣F)=0.026.\n$$\n\n- Since $46%$ of children with scoliosis are female, we have\n\n$$\nP(F∣C)=0.46.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that a randomly chosen child who practices one sport has scoliosis, which is represented as $P(C∣{S}_{1}).$\n\nUsing Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F∣C) & =\\frac{P(C∣F)P(F)}{P(C)} \\\\ P(F∣C) & =\\frac{P(C∣F)P(F)}{P(C∣{S}_{0})P({S}_{0})+P(C∣{S}_{1})P({S}_{1})+P(C∣{S}_{2})P({S}_{2})} \\\\ 0.46 & =\\frac{(0.026)(0.48)}{(0.25)(0.025)+P(C∣{S}_{1})(0.3)+(0.028)(0.45)} \\\\ 0.46 & =\\frac{0.0125}{0.0189+0.3P(C∣{S}_{1})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $P(C∣{S}_{1}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.46(0.0189+0.3P(C∣{S}_{1})) & =0.0125 \\\\ 0.0189+0.3P(C∣{S}_{1}) & =\\frac{0.0125}{0.46} \\\\ 0.3P(C∣{S}_{1}) & =\\frac{0.0125}{0.46}-0.0189 \\\\ P(C∣{S}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{0.3}(\\frac{0.0125}{0.46}-0.0189) \\\\ P(C∣{S}_{1}) & ≈0.028\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c97eb869-625e-551f-be3b-c0ff2ec27876" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a2ac414e-15b9-5ce9-93e3-a7f2a6d829da" "answer-c97eb869-625e-551f-be3b-c0ff2ec27876" "answer-8a26048a-fd81-56ee-8af6-bd08ebb325b0" "answer-50e9c58b-4fb9-5497-9482-e8f285727015" "answer-5b9c5c15-f6a2-5b4a-a895-22168d05307d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2ac414e-15b9-5ce9-93e3-a7f2a6d829da" :answer/id #uuid "a2ac414e-15b9-5ce9-93e3-a7f2a6d829da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.019" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c97eb869-625e-551f-be3b-c0ff2ec27876" :answer/id #uuid "c97eb869-625e-551f-be3b-c0ff2ec27876" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.028" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a26048a-fd81-56ee-8af6-bd08ebb325b0" :answer/id #uuid "8a26048a-fd81-56ee-8af6-bd08ebb325b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.047" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-50e9c58b-4fb9-5497-9482-e8f285727015" :answer/id #uuid "50e9c58b-4fb9-5497-9482-e8f285727015" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.055" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b9c5c15-f6a2-5b4a-a895-22168d05307d" :answer/id #uuid "5b9c5c15-f6a2-5b4a-a895-22168d05307d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.095" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-4a76ab2b-fb4c-5063-aa81-3107b8d38d69" :activity/id #uuid "4a76ab2b-fb4c-5063-aa81-3107b8d38d69" :activity/title "Extending Bayes' Theorem" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048270 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-5af77563-9292-5cfd-aaa2-e0647be6b4b1" "step-da95ad9e-2b99-5840-9da1-16c4078a085a" "step-964218e8-bf1c-559e-ad24-e50227ec5968" "step-fce198a3-2fe3-5172-8c78-1731bf8adc70" "step-39ce452f-966f-5775-99e0-20fb8ca0eef9"] :activity/first-step "step-5af77563-9292-5cfd-aaa2-e0647be6b4b1" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-5af77563-9292-5cfd-aaa2-e0647be6b4b1" :step/id #uuid "5af77563-9292-5cfd-aaa2-e0647be6b4b1" :step/content "question-9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e" :step/next "step-da95ad9e-2b99-5840-9da1-16c4078a085a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-da95ad9e-2b99-5840-9da1-16c4078a085a" :step/id #uuid "da95ad9e-2b99-5840-9da1-16c4078a085a" :step/content 17592186487364 :step/next "step-964218e8-bf1c-559e-ad24-e50227ec5968" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-964218e8-bf1c-559e-ad24-e50227ec5968" :step/id #uuid "964218e8-bf1c-559e-ad24-e50227ec5968" :step/content "question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc" :step/next "step-fce198a3-2fe3-5172-8c78-1731bf8adc70" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fce198a3-2fe3-5172-8c78-1731bf8adc70" :step/id #uuid "fce198a3-2fe3-5172-8c78-1731bf8adc70" :step/content 17592186487402 :step/next "step-39ce452f-966f-5775-99e0-20fb8ca0eef9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-39ce452f-966f-5775-99e0-20fb8ca0eef9" :step/id #uuid "39ce452f-966f-5775-99e0-20fb8ca0eef9" :step/content "question-1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e" :question/id #uuid "9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e"] ["question-9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-147885"] ["question-9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e" :question/problem "The disjoint union ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔{A}_{3}⊔{A}_{4}$ of events ${A}_{1},{A}_{2},{A}_{3},{A}_{4}$ covers the entire sample space. Compute $P({A}_{2}|B)$ given the following probabilities:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P(B|{A}_{1})=0.25, & P({A}_{1})=0.28 \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{2})=0.3, &  \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{3})=0.28, & P({A}_{3})=0.18 \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{4})=0.1, & P({A}_{4})=0.22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound your answer to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e" :question/worked-solution "If the disjoint union ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔…⊔{A}_{n}$ covers the entire sample space, Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability gives us the following:\n\n$$\nP({A}_{k}|B)=\\frac{P(B|{A}_{k})P({A}_{k})}{P(B)}=\\frac{P(B|{A}_{k})P({A}_{k})}{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}P(B|{A}_{i})P({A}_{i})}\n$$\n\nwhere $k=1,2,…,n.$\n\nIn our case, $n=4,$ and ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔{A}_{3}⊔{A}_{4}$ covers the entire sample space. Consequently, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}_{1})+P({A}_{2})+P({A}_{3})+P({A}_{4})=1.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}_{2}) & =1-(P({A}_{1})+P({A}_{3})+P({A}_{4})) \\\\  & =1-(0.28+0.18+0.22) \\\\  & =0.32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}_{2}|B) & =\\frac{P(B|{A}_{2})P({A}_{2})}{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}P(B|{A}_{i})P({A}_{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(B|{A}_{2})P({A}_{2})}{P(B|{A}_{1})P({A}_{1})+P(B|{A}_{2})P({A}_{2})+P(B|{A}_{3})P({A}_{3})+P(B|{A}_{4})P({A}_{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.3)(0.32)}{(0.25)(0.28)+(0.3)(0.32)+(0.28)(0.18)+(0.1)(0.22)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.096}{0.2384} \\\\  & ≈0.403.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2"] ["answer-3abf36e3-3cf2-5339-8e78-9d57d7acb48a" :answer/id #uuid "3abf36e3-3cf2-5339-8e78-9d57d7acb48a"] ["answer-3abf36e3-3cf2-5339-8e78-9d57d7acb48a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3abf36e3-3cf2-5339-8e78-9d57d7acb48a" :answer/value "0.286"] ["answer-408cef73-e79b-5f84-909b-bb78b0af2709" :answer/id #uuid "408cef73-e79b-5f84-909b-bb78b0af2709"] ["answer-408cef73-e79b-5f84-909b-bb78b0af2709" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-408cef73-e79b-5f84-909b-bb78b0af2709" :answer/value "0.322"] ["answer-161fb25c-96cf-5b02-8d7d-25af5ca8f28a" :answer/id #uuid "161fb25c-96cf-5b02-8d7d-25af5ca8f28a"] ["answer-161fb25c-96cf-5b02-8d7d-25af5ca8f28a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-161fb25c-96cf-5b02-8d7d-25af5ca8f28a" :answer/value "0.365"] ["answer-cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d" :answer/id #uuid "cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d"] ["answer-cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d" :answer/value "0.403"] ["answer-c7987182-3703-5340-83e1-52554f33e28f" :answer/id #uuid "c7987182-3703-5340-83e1-52554f33e28f"] ["answer-c7987182-3703-5340-83e1-52554f33e28f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c7987182-3703-5340-83e1-52554f33e28f" :answer/value "0.444"] ["answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/correct "answer-cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d"] ["answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/choices "answer-3abf36e3-3cf2-5339-8e78-9d57d7acb48a"] ["answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/choices "answer-408cef73-e79b-5f84-909b-bb78b0af2709"] ["answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/choices "answer-161fb25c-96cf-5b02-8d7d-25af5ca8f28a"] ["answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/choices "answer-cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d"] ["answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/choices "answer-c7987182-3703-5340-83e1-52554f33e28f"] ["question-9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2"] [17592186166847 :knowledge-point/questions "question-9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e"] ["question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc" :question/id #uuid "095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc"] ["question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc" :question/math-academy-id "q-148082"] ["question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc" :question/problem "A medical center is investigating the correlation between scoliosis and sports practice in a sample of children.\n\n- $25%$ of children in the sample don't practice sports, and $3%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\n- $30%$ of children in the sample practice one sport, and $2.5%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\n- $45%$ of children in the sample practice two sports, and $3.3%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\nIf $52%$ of children in the entire sample are female, and $2%$ of female children have scoliosis, what is the probability that a randomly chosen child with scoliosis is female? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc" :question/worked-solution "Let $F$ be the event that a child is female, $C$ be the event that a child has scoliosis, and ${S}_{0},{S}_{1},{S}_{2}$ be the event that a child practice $0,$ $1,$ or $2$ sports, respectively.\n\nLet's break down the information given in the problem statement:\n\n- From the bullet points, we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P({S}_{0})=0.25 &  & P(C|{S}_{0})=0.03 \\\\  & P({S}_{1})=0.30 &  & P(C|{S}_{1})=0.025 \\\\  & P({S}_{2})=0.45 &  & P(C|{S}_{2})=0.033\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe disjoint union ${S}_{0}⊔{S}_{1}⊔{S}_{2}$ covers the entire sample space, and we have\n\n$$\nP({S}_{0})+P({S}_{1})+P({S}_{2})=0.25+0.30+0.45=1.\n$$\n\n- Since $52%$ of children in the entire sample are female, we have\n\n$$\nP(F)=0.52.\n$$\n\n- Since $2%$ of females have scoliosis, we have\n\n$$\nP(C|F)=0.02.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that a randomly chosen child with scoliosis is female, which is represented as $P(F|C).$ \n\nUsing Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F|C) & =\\frac{P(C|F)P(F)}{P(C)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(C|F)P(F)}{P(C|{S}_{0})P({S}_{0})+P(C|{S}_{1})P({S}_{1})+P(C|{S}_{2})P({S}_{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.02)(0.52)}{(0.03)(0.25)+(0.025)(0.3)+(0.033)(0.45)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.0104}{0.0299} \\\\  & ≈0.348,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/id #uuid "af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320"] ["answer-144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460" :answer/id #uuid "144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460"] ["answer-144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460" :answer/value "0.348"] ["answer-39018054-1073-5cec-87c0-3be506864193" :answer/id #uuid "39018054-1073-5cec-87c0-3be506864193"] ["answer-39018054-1073-5cec-87c0-3be506864193" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-39018054-1073-5cec-87c0-3be506864193" :answer/value "0.415"] ["answer-7aae2ee8-a81d-50e2-98ea-e2df978f83a9" :answer/id #uuid "7aae2ee8-a81d-50e2-98ea-e2df978f83a9"] ["answer-7aae2ee8-a81d-50e2-98ea-e2df978f83a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7aae2ee8-a81d-50e2-98ea-e2df978f83a9" :answer/value "0.48"] ["answer-85700ac7-cad1-590c-a143-b418ccc70b5b" :answer/id #uuid "85700ac7-cad1-590c-a143-b418ccc70b5b"] ["answer-85700ac7-cad1-590c-a143-b418ccc70b5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-85700ac7-cad1-590c-a143-b418ccc70b5b" :answer/value "0.52"] ["answer-7dd4d43d-b30b-5f97-8032-3941bf17d1fb" :answer/id #uuid "7dd4d43d-b30b-5f97-8032-3941bf17d1fb"] ["answer-7dd4d43d-b30b-5f97-8032-3941bf17d1fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7dd4d43d-b30b-5f97-8032-3941bf17d1fb" :answer/value "0.552"] ["answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/correct "answer-144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460"] ["answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/choices "answer-144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460"] ["answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/choices "answer-39018054-1073-5cec-87c0-3be506864193"] ["answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/choices "answer-7aae2ee8-a81d-50e2-98ea-e2df978f83a9"] ["answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/choices "answer-85700ac7-cad1-590c-a143-b418ccc70b5b"] ["answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/choices "answer-7dd4d43d-b30b-5f97-8032-3941bf17d1fb"] ["question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320"] [17592186166877 :knowledge-point/questions "question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc"] ["question-1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe" :question/id #uuid "1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe"] ["question-1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-148271"] ["question-1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe" :question/problem "A medical center is investigating the correlation between scoliosis and sports practice in a sample of children.\n\n- $25%$ of children in the sample don't practice sports, and $2.5%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\n- $30%$ of children in the sample practice one sport.\n\n- $45%$ of children in the sample practice two sports, and $2.8%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\nIf $48%$ of children in the entire sample are female, $2.6%$ of female children have scoliosis, and $46%$ of children with scoliosis are female, what is the probability that a randomly chosen child who practices one sport has scoliosis? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe" :question/worked-solution "Let $F$ be the event that a child is female, $C$ be the event that a child has scoliosis, and ${S}_{0},{S}_{1},{S}_{2}$ be the event that a child practices $0,$ $1,$ or $2$ sports, respectively.\n\nLet's break down the information given in the problem statement:\n\n- From the bullet points, we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P({S}_{0})=0.25 &  & P(C∣{S}_{0})=0.025 \\\\  & P({S}_{1})=0.30 \\\\  & P({S}_{2})=0.45 &  & P(C∣{S}_{2})=0.028\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe disjoint union ${S}_{0}⊔{S}_{1}⊔{S}_{2}$ covers the entire sample space, and we have\n\n$$\nP({S}_{0})+P({S}_{1})+P({S}_{2})=0.25+0.30+0.45=1.\n$$\n\n- Since $48%$ of students in the entire sample are female, we have\n\n$$\nP(F)=0.48.\n$$\n\n- Since $2.6%$ of females have scoliosis, we have\n\n$$\nP(C∣F)=0.026.\n$$\n\n- Since $46%$ of children with scoliosis are female, we have\n\n$$\nP(F∣C)=0.46.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that a randomly chosen child who practices one sport has scoliosis, which is represented as $P(C∣{S}_{1}).$\n\nUsing Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F∣C) & =\\frac{P(C∣F)P(F)}{P(C)} \\\\ P(F∣C) & =\\frac{P(C∣F)P(F)}{P(C∣{S}_{0})P({S}_{0})+P(C∣{S}_{1})P({S}_{1})+P(C∣{S}_{2})P({S}_{2})} \\\\ 0.46 & =\\frac{(0.026)(0.48)}{(0.25)(0.025)+P(C∣{S}_{1})(0.3)+(0.028)(0.45)} \\\\ 0.46 & =\\frac{0.0125}{0.0189+0.3P(C∣{S}_{1})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $P(C∣{S}_{1}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.46(0.0189+0.3P(C∣{S}_{1})) & =0.0125 \\\\ 0.0189+0.3P(C∣{S}_{1}) & =\\frac{0.0125}{0.46} \\\\ 0.3P(C∣{S}_{1}) & =\\frac{0.0125}{0.46}-0.0189 \\\\ P(C∣{S}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{0.3}(\\frac{0.0125}{0.46}-0.0189) \\\\ P(C∣{S}_{1}) & ≈0.028\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places."] ["question-1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4"] ["answer-a2ac414e-15b9-5ce9-93e3-a7f2a6d829da" :answer/id #uuid "a2ac414e-15b9-5ce9-93e3-a7f2a6d829da"] ["answer-a2ac414e-15b9-5ce9-93e3-a7f2a6d829da" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a2ac414e-15b9-5ce9-93e3-a7f2a6d829da" :answer/value "0.019"] ["answer-c97eb869-625e-551f-be3b-c0ff2ec27876" :answer/id #uuid "c97eb869-625e-551f-be3b-c0ff2ec27876"] ["answer-c97eb869-625e-551f-be3b-c0ff2ec27876" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c97eb869-625e-551f-be3b-c0ff2ec27876" :answer/value "0.028"] ["answer-8a26048a-fd81-56ee-8af6-bd08ebb325b0" :answer/id #uuid "8a26048a-fd81-56ee-8af6-bd08ebb325b0"] ["answer-8a26048a-fd81-56ee-8af6-bd08ebb325b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8a26048a-fd81-56ee-8af6-bd08ebb325b0" :answer/value "0.047"] ["answer-50e9c58b-4fb9-5497-9482-e8f285727015" :answer/id #uuid "50e9c58b-4fb9-5497-9482-e8f285727015"] ["answer-50e9c58b-4fb9-5497-9482-e8f285727015" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-50e9c58b-4fb9-5497-9482-e8f285727015" :answer/value "0.055"] ["answer-5b9c5c15-f6a2-5b4a-a895-22168d05307d" :answer/id #uuid "5b9c5c15-f6a2-5b4a-a895-22168d05307d"] ["answer-5b9c5c15-f6a2-5b4a-a895-22168d05307d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5b9c5c15-f6a2-5b4a-a895-22168d05307d" :answer/value "0.095"] ["answer-field-2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4" :answer-field/correct "answer-c97eb869-625e-551f-be3b-c0ff2ec27876"] ["answer-field-2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4" :answer-field/choices "answer-a2ac414e-15b9-5ce9-93e3-a7f2a6d829da"] ["answer-field-2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4" :answer-field/choices "answer-c97eb869-625e-551f-be3b-c0ff2ec27876"] ["answer